            <ArticleTitle>An unusual case of prolonged tinnitus following low-dose amitriptyline.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>574-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/0269881107082126</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on a case of unilateral tinnitus after a short course of low-dose amitriptyline for neuralgic foot pain. This has been described in the literature previously at much higher doses and is associated with prolonged administration; we present our case with a review of the current literature in-order to raise awareness of this possible complication of anti-depressant therapy. We also propose a novel hypothesis for the pharmacological basis of amitriptyline-induced tinnitus.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
